  "notes": "Traditions of Innovation option, University Park track (126 credits) — one of two options (the other, Writing and Literature in Context, has no published Suggested Academic Plan). Like every B.A., English carries substantial open electives and 'Concentration Course' slots tied to four literary-era groupings (Medieval-16th C., 16th-18th C., 19th C., 20th C.-Present) that aren't individually enumerated in the bulletin's course list, so those and the World Language sequence (varies by language, no fixed PSU code) are modeled as unenforced slots, same convention as CMPSC's elective pools. 'etm' marks the courses everything else in the sequence assumes are done (intro writing, ENGL 200/201). For 2022-23 through 2024-25, the curriculum was 123 credits total (not 126) — LA 83 and the LA 283 Sophomore Seminar slot (1.5cr each) were not yet part of the plan. Re-verified against bulletins.psu.edu's own program-requirements PDF (english-ba_programrequirementstext.pdf) for a real handbook-depth pass -- no separate English department handbook beyond the bulletin could be found published anywhere, so this is a bulletin-only major. Confirmed the real credit-bucket math: Common Requirements (ENGL 200/201 3cr + ENGL 487W/494H 3cr + 18cr Supporting, >=9cr at 300/400 level) + Traditions of Innovation Option (12cr, one 3cr course per era: Medieval-16th C., 16th-18th C., 19th C., 20th C.-Present) = 36cr major total -- this plan's 10 generic Concentration-style slots (6 untyped + 4 regex-matched 400-level) sum to exactly 30cr, matching the bulletin's 18+12=30cr combined exactly. The department doesn't publish an enumerable era-to-course list (adviser-driven), so the undifferentiated pool is a genuine open requirement, not a data gap. Also found and fixed a real, previously-unenforced mutual exclusion in the shared engl_catalog.json: each course's own description states 'A student may take only one course for credit from ENGL 202A, 202B, 202C, and 202D' -- added as excludes on all 4 variants (harmless for this plan alone, since it only ever schedules one ENGL 202 pick, but now also protected against a multi-major/minor merge double-count).",
